WEBVTT

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.513
Here's Gem Island, the starter game,

00:00:05.513 --> 00:00:07.191
open on the Game workspace.

00:00:07.231 --> 00:00:09.774
Click a gem in the 3D View to select it.

00:00:09.774 --> 00:00:11.777
The Outliner highlights it too.

00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:14.905
To move it, pick the Move tool in the toolbar.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:18.877
Drag the green arrow to slide the gem along that axis,

00:00:18.877 --> 00:00:21.205
here closer to where the player starts.

00:00:21.767 --> 00:00:23.387
Now give it some behaviour.

00:00:23.427 --> 00:00:25.413
In the Properties, the Object tab's

00:00:25.413 --> 00:00:27.822
Game panel lists the gem's components:

00:00:27.909 --> 00:00:29.819
Collectible came with the starter.

00:00:29.906 --> 00:00:31.630
Click Add Component.

00:00:32.333 --> 00:00:33.993
Choose Spin, under Motion.

00:00:33.993 --> 00:00:36.716
It turns the object while the game runs.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:39.839
Scroll down the Properties to Spin's settings.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.034
Set its Speed to three.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.746
The gems already turn slowly;

00:00:43.746 --> 00:00:45.215
this one will whirl.

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:48.019
To see the level the way the game draws it,

00:00:48.019 --> 00:00:50.336
turn on Game in the 3D View's header.

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:52.321
This is the Scene view:

00:00:52.408 --> 00:00:55.259
the game's own renderer, without playing.

00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:58.893
Selecting, moving and zooming all work as usual here.

00:00:58.979 --> 00:01:00.588
Scroll to get closer.

00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:03.089
Now press F5 to play.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.200
The game runs right here, in place of the 3D View.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:08.457
It opens on its title screen.

00:01:08.543 --> 00:01:09.502
Click Play.

00:01:09.542 --> 00:01:12.729
That click also hands your mouse and keyboard to the game.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.902
There's the gem where you moved it,

00:01:14.902 --> 00:01:16.685
spinning faster than the others.

00:01:16.829 --> 00:01:19.587
W, A, S and D walk over to collect it.

00:01:20.167 --> 00:01:23.482
Press Shift and Escape to take the mouse back from the game.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:26.819
F8 stops the game, and the 3D View is back,

00:01:26.819 --> 00:01:28.509
ready for the next change.

00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:30.019
That's the loop:

00:01:30.019 --> 00:01:33.130
change something in Blender, press F5 to try it,

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:35.447
F8 to stop, and go again.
